  <static seed="78" source="Library/TCNJ/TCNJ_MatrixLinearTransformation/problem23.pg">
    <statement><p>Let <m>T</m> be a linear transformation from 
<m>{\mathbb R}^3</m> to
<m>{\mathbb R}^3</m> .</p>
<p>Determine whether or not <m>T</m> is onto in each of the following situations:</p>
<p><ol>
<li>
<p>Suppose <m>T(a) = u</m>,  <m>T(b) = v</m>, <m>T(c)=u+v</m>, where 
<m>a, b, c, u,v</m> are vectors in <m>{\mathbb R}^3</m>.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Suppose <m>T</m> is a one-to-one function</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Suppose <m>T(1, 4, -2)=u</m>,  <m>T(1, 3, 2)=v</m>,
<m>T(2, 8, 0)=u+v</m>.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<ol label="A.">
<li>
<p>T is not onto.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>T is onto.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>There is not enough information to tell</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
